  "scopeText": "This is a prospective input amendment, not a setup/test result. Before authoring the supervisor, repeated read-only probes found the inherited loopback proxy port differs between separate exec contexts. Package-proxy observations changed only the port (35633→39643); ordinary HTTP proxy observations changed35417→41601 and SOCKS proxy41343→40435. All four fixed npm values stayed exact, both case variants agree, and ordinary HTTP(S) proxies equal the package proxy in each corresponding observation. The fixed NO_PROXY value is identical across ordinary and package aliases. No credentials, URL path/query/fragment or nonloopback hostname was observed. These observations invalidate treating the old complete environment digest as a reusable fixed input; the old value remains retained history.\nOnly the listed port components may be supplied from the inherited execution context. Preserve the original environment's actual network route; do not create a proxy, replace it with another address, clear it to obtain direct network access, change an allowlist, or use these settings to bypass egress/access controls. Unknown keys, inconsistent aliases, changed fixed values, credentials or changed URL components refuse before any stage. Different HTTP and SOCKS ports are expected separate admitted groups, not conflicting aliases.\nCapture the exact original mapping once, retain its per-value identities and unambiguous full canonical hash, and derive all Git/download/pnpm/build child environments from that same captured snapshot. Verify the original mapping is unchanged at each phase boundary; do not recapture a later tool invocation or rebind a failed stage. If an inherited port expires or any network operation fails, that stage remains failed with no automatic retry or alternate route. The four bootstrap stages must run in one supervisor invocation; their separate one-attempt deadlines remain600/120/600/180 seconds. Preserve the existing command-local sanitation and nine explicit PNPM_CONFIG selections, task XDG directories, fixed HOME/CODEX_HOME and source/tool/lock/patch identities.\nAdd the actually derived fixed prefix config /home/agent/.local/etc/npmrc to absent-config checks. It was read-only observed absent and is derived from the fixed18-byte prefix; do not create or alter it. All original listed user/global config absence checks remain.\nThis amendment supersedes only cross-invocation fixed use of inheritedPackageConfigCanonicalSha256 in bfc885 and the corresponding sentence in its scope. All source selections, four stage commands and budgets, pnpm integrity, shell and tool pins, no-real-provider/SDK-import gate, same97 tests, old five unused test/guard budgets, semantic RED before producer, runner650-line cap, complete R2/custody/raw/cleanup requirements, no frozen-PR/CI/main/release actions remain exact. It authorizes no test or provider import by itself.\nPublish this amendment with an append-only Plan29 on the own branch, exact7e6 parent, immediate create→push with force=false. Complete independent actual published readback precedes any supervisor postimage authoring or selection. Exact runner/binding R2 still precedes local materialization/execution. At amendment preparation no supervisor, setup, test or producer has been authored or executed."
}
